# Navigation Shortcuts

Elevators (and future bus stops / tunnels / portals) plug into the existing route system as **shortcut hops** — single zero-walk edges with a fixed time cost. With the dev "Use shortcuts" toggle ON, the composer always evaluates both walking and elevator routes and picks the **strict shortest** by default. A second dev toggle "Prefer elevators" flips that policy: take the lift whenever it is **valid** (passes vertical filters), even if walking would be shorter. Phase 1 ships **elevators only** but the schema and runtime are intentionally type-agnostic so new shortcut types land via config alone.

> **Status: v1 (committed baseline).** End-to-end for guided routes (seat / POI / quiet / exit nav) with the dev toggles on; CU unchanged. **Seat + elevator:** post-hop corridor uses the same `plan_route(section)` graph as non-shortcut seat nav (`corridor_section`), with floor trim + branch rejoin (see below). POI/quiet/exit still use `plan_route_to_position` unless the client sends `corridorSection`. Further tuning is expected — known limitations stay at the bottom.

### CU elevator travel via POI coins (separate path)

Production **CU** can move between floors at an elevator **without** the dev toggles or `ShortcutTraversalService`:

1. Player opens an elevator **coin** (proximity pill or 3D click) → `PoiInfoCard` **Use elevator** + floor buttons (`metadata.elevator_ride` from `coins_loader` + `elevator_data.json`).
2. Web sends **`poiTeleport`** to the destination NavShortcuts Xform `prim_path` (same nodes as `shortcuts.json`).
3. Kit `poi_routes` teleports via `TeleportService` (spawn rotation + localized `arrivalLabel` from the shortcuts node).

This reuses **`shortcuts.json` + `nav_shortcuts_layer.usda`** as the coordinate source but is **not** a route-hop: no `shortcutTraversalBegin`, no post-hop NavMesh recompose. Full workflow: **`poi-coins.mdc`** § Elevator ride; arrival/rotation: **`poi-teleport.mdc`**.

