## Data layout

### USD: `nav_shortcuts_layer.usda`

Single sublayer at `kit-app-template-main/source/data/scenes/sublayers/nav_shortcuts_layer.usda`, included from `main_scene.usda`. Each shortcut node is a plain `Xform` whose **world translation** is both:

- The walk-up target the NavMesh route ends at (entrance), and
- The teleport spawn pose when arriving via the connected node (exit).

Path convention is `/World/NavShortcuts/<group_id>/<node_id>`:

```
/World/NavShortcuts
├── elevator_1/                    # Section A elevator
│   ├── floor_0                    # ground
│   ├── floor_1
│   └── floor_2
└── elevator_2/                    # Section R elevator (only floors 1-2)
    ├── floor_1
    └── floor_2
```

Add new groups by creating Xforms here and mirroring `(group_id, node_id, primPath)` in `shortcuts.json`. The Xform's translation must sit on the NavMesh on every floor it represents — `surface: navmesh` in the JSON is a contract.

### JSON: `shortcuts.json`

Lives at `kit-app-template-main/source/data/shortcuts.json`. Schema:

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "elevator_1",                       // matches /World/NavShortcuts/<id>
      "type": "elevator",                       // future: "bus", "tunnel", "portal"
      "i18nKey": "shortcuts.elevatorSectionA",
      "labelEn": "Section A elevator",
      "traversalSeconds": 4.0,                  // ride time (tune vs stairs)
      "waitSeconds": 1.0,                       // wait/dwell time
      "servesSections": [],                     // seat sections this group may serve;
                                                // empty/absent → POIs / generic dests only
      "edges": "all",                           // or [["floor_0","floor_1"], …]
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "floor_0",
          "level": 0,
          "labelEn": "Section A — Ground floor",
          "i18nKey": "shortcuts.sectionA.floor0",
          "primPath": "/World/NavShortcuts/elevator_1/floor_0",
          "surface": "navmesh"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

`edges: "all"` produces a fully-connected graph between every pair of nodes in the group. Use an explicit list when an elevator skips floors or a bus route is one-way.

`traversalSeconds + waitSeconds` is mapped to hop cost in cm via `shortcut_router.constants.DEFAULT_WALK_CM_PER_SEC` (130.0, ≈ 1.3 m/s). Example: **5 s** total → **650 cm** walk-equivalent per hop — lower values make the lift win more often against long stair NavMesh paths; raise them if lifts feel over-selected.

`servesSections` is the **single source of truth** for which seat sections may use a group. Letters are case-insensitive (uppercased on load); unknown / typo'd letters silently fall through (the section gate just won't match). Today: `elevator_1.servesSections = []` (POIs / `quiet_zone_03` only), `elevator_2.servesSections = ["P","S"]` (upper-bowl P + S via the OP/RS branch chain). Wiring a new elevator that serves new sections is a JSON-only edit — see "Hard rules" above for the section-gate semantics.

