## Event contract

All registered via `register_outbound_events` so the messaging core knows about them.

| Event | Direction | Payload | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `shortcutsToggle` | web → Kit | `{active: bool}` | "Use shortcuts" dev menu button. Triggers `set_shortcuts_active` and reloads the router. |
| `shortcutsStatus` | Kit → web | `{active: bool}` | Backend confirms current state — drives `setShortcutsActive` so reconnects/world-state-sync stay in sync. |
| `shortcutsPreferToggle` | web → Kit | `{active: bool}` | "Prefer elevators" dev menu button. Triggers `set_prefer_shortcuts`, which forces a `recalc_now()` on every active route already using shortcuts. |
| `shortcutsPreferStatus` | Kit → web | `{active: bool}` | Backend confirms current prefer state — drives `setPreferShortcutsActive`. |
| `shortcutTraversalBegin` | Kit → web | `{routeId, fromPos, toPos, groupId, type, fromLabel, toLabel, traversalSeconds}` | Player has reached the elevator entrance. Frontend fades out. |
| `shortcutTraversalProceed` | web → Kit | `{routeId}` | Frontend's `onFadeOutComplete`. Kit unblocks teleport. |
| `shortcutTraversalComplete` | Kit → web | `{routeId}` | Teleport done, fade-in already requested via the existing `viewTransitionReady` channel. |
| `shortcutTraversalError` | Kit → web | `{routeId, error?}` | Teleport failed. Frontend should still release the fade overlay. |
| `playerPathClassChange` | internal | `{prev, next, segIdx, routeId}` | Auto-mover → `ShortcutTraversalService`. The trigger that starts the whole sequence. |

Safety cap: if the frontend never replies with `shortcutTraversalProceed`, `_FADE_TIMEOUT_SEC = 1.5` proceeds with the teleport anyway. Useful for headless dev.

